"id":8664832009,
"title":"Nicaragua - Cafe Diego",
"handle":"nicaragua-cafe-diego",
"body_html":"<p><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><span>When we talk about Nicaragua Café Diego, we aren't just discussing a screen size or a cup score. We are looking at a story of endurance. This coffee is the result of a direct-trade relationship with farmer Diego Chavarria in the Matagalpa region—a story so compelling it inspired the documentary Café Diego: The Cost of a Dream.</span><br><br><span>Historically, Matagalpa has been the \"Coffee Capital\" of Nicaragua since the mid-19th century. The region's high altitude and old shade canopy create a microclimate that slows bean maturation. This slow growth is exactly what develops the dense cellular structure we look for in a specialty-grade Strictly High Grown (SHG) bean.</span></p>\n<p>Café Diego is a direct trade coffee with a creamy body; clean, sweet, citric acidity and a caramel sweetness; smooth and aromatic.</p>",
"published_at":"2026-09-18T15:31:09-04:00",
"created_at":"2017-01-06T13:10:32-05:00",
